/**
  @page examples-mmg-mesh_adaptation Adapting to a size field
  @brief Prescribe local edge lengths and inspect the resulting mesh density.

  @tableofcontents
  @m_footernavigation

  @section examples-mmg-adapt-intro A spatially varying target

  On the unit square, prescribe the scalar edge-size field
  @f[
    h(x,y)=0.05+0.15x.
  @f]
  The requested size is smallest at the left edge and largest at the right
  edge. This known field isolates the remeshing operation before a PDE error
  estimator is introduced. MMG inserts, removes and moves vertices to approach
  the prescribed sizes under its geometric and gradation constraints.

  @section examples-mmg-adapt-workflow Construct and pass the size field

  The initial mesh has 81 vertices and 128 triangles.

  @snippet MMG/MeshAdaptation.cpp mmg-adapt-setup

  A scalar nodal field supplies the target edge lengths. `MMG::Adapt::adapt`
  consumes that field while changing the mesh. Its space is scoped to this
  call; construct new spaces on the resulting topology before subsequent
  field interpolation or PDE solves.

  @snippet MMG/MeshAdaptation.cpp mmg-adapt-call

  @section examples-mmg-adapt-behavior Inspect density and domain preservation

  @m_class{rodin-mesh-stages}

  @parblock
  @image html MMGAdaptation-before.png "Mesh before adaptation, with the same plotting scale."
  @image html MMGAdaptation-after.png "Mesh after adaptation, with the same plotting scale."
  @endparblock

  The size field is an input to remeshing. A solve–estimate–adapt loop also
  needs a specified error indicator, its conversion to positive target sizes,
  field transfer and a stopping criterion. Each of those choices affects the
  numerical approximation and should be checked for the intended PDE.

  @section examples-mmg-adapt-run Build and run

  Build the `MeshAdaptation` target. It writes the input and output meshes as
  `Before.medit.mesh` and `After.medit.mesh`, along with triangle CSV files
  used for the figure. The program checks positive triangle areas and unit
  total area with tolerance @f$10^{-10}@f$.

  The complete program is available in @ref MMG/MeshAdaptation.cpp "MeshAdaptation.cpp".

  @section examples-mmg-adapt-see-also Continue

  - @ref examples-mmg-mesh_optimization "Quality optimization"
  - @ref examples-mmg-behavior "Required geometry and level-set cuts"
  - @ref guides-numerical-contracts "Field and mesh lifetimes"

  @example MMG/MeshAdaptation.cpp
  @m_footernavigation
*/
